      <title>Section 41 - Lagrange Multipliers with One Constraint</title>
      <objectives>
  <p><em>Learning Objectives</em></p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Use Lagrange multipliers to find the maximum and minimum of a function of two variables.
    </li>
    <li>
      Use Lagrange multipliers to find the maximum and minimum of a function of three variables.
    </li>
  </ul>
</objectives>

